Fungal skin infections such as ringworm (tinea) are common in hot, humid weather. Many people find the rash fades with a cream and then returns a few weeks later.

## Common reasons it returns

- Stopping treatment as soon as the itch settles, before the infection has cleared.
- Creams that contain a steroid. They reduce redness at first but can make the infection spread and harder to treat.
- Family members with the same rash, or shared towels and clothes.
- Clothes that stay damp with sweat for long periods.

## What helps

See a dermatologist before starting another cream, and bring the creams you have already used. Finish the full course you are given, even after the rash fades, and wash and dry clothes and towels well.

